  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 3 of KAFKA FIELD NOTES. Kafka does not order your topic. It orders a partition, and your key is what decides which one a record lands in — everything else follows from that. 10 pages of field notes: log mechanics and offsets, murmur2 partitioning, why adding partitions is a one-way destructive door, RF vs ISR vs acks, cooperative rebalancing, compaction rules, and the failure modes that look like durability but aren't. Save it before your next topic design review.",
